{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:22-5","provision":"BCO 22-5","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"22-5","title":"Section 22-5","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/22-5/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/22-5","current_text":{"html":"<p>In order to provide necessary changes in pastorates, a temporary relation may be established between a church and a minister called Stated Supply. If a church is unable to secure a regular pastor or a Stated Supply, then the Session with approval of Presbytery may establish a temporary relation between the church and a licentiate called Student Supply or Ruling Elder Supply.</p>","text":"In order to provide necessary changes in pastorates, a temporary relation may be established between a church and a minister called Stated Supply. If a church is unable to secure a regular pastor or a Stated Supply, then the Session with approval of Presbytery may establish a temporary relation between the church and a licentiate called Student Supply or Ruling Elder Supply."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":"bco:22","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":21,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:22-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Minister from another denomination serving as stated supply","year":1992,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-5--inquiry:inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.md:occ-23bdbaf4191b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"A minister from another denomination licensed by a PCA presbytery may serve as stated supply but may not administer sacraments unless his denomination has fraternal relations with the PCA or his sacramental views are consistent with PCA standards.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga20_1992__ci01.md"}]},{"id":"bco:22-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Antioch Session v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":1994,"disposition":"not_sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-5--case:cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md:occ-97836142c53f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["licensure","creation","age of earth","flood (local vs. universal)","divorce and remarriage","church office qualifications","stated supply","system of doctrine","theonomy","presbytery jurisdiction over membership"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1992-9a"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Antioch Session challenged Peterson’s licensure based on his prior divorce, creation and local-flood views, reversal of a committee recommendation, and close vote; it also challenged his regular preaching before licensure. The SJC rejected the licensure specifications because Presbytery had thoroughly examined repentance and doctrinal adherence, and no definitive PCA standard required exclusion on these facts. It sustained the pre-licensure supply issue under BCO 19-1, 22-5, and 22-6 and enjoined greater future circumspection. The licensure remained undisturbed; the ruling was expressly case-specific."}},{"id":"bco:22-5--case:cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Parks et al. v. Central Carolina Presbytery","year":1993,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-5--case:cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.md:occ-4fc6487f09f7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":66},"excerpt":"…year, renewable at the request of the Session and at the review of Presbytery (BCO 22-5,6).","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga21_1993__1992-05.md"}],"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1992-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Complainants challenged a Session plan under which most elders voluntarily resigned, the Session granted severance and benefits to its former pastor, proposed about a year with an interim pastor before a permanent call, and contemplated revising local bylaws. The SJC denied all four items. It held that the BCO permitted jointly considered voluntary resignations, that severance concerned resignation and the budget rather than a pastoral call, and that the plan and bylaw proposal were not themselves unconstitutional. Any later call still had to follow the BCO without undue delay, and local bylaws had to remain consistent with it."}},{"id":"bco:22-5--overture:ga37_2009:4","record_id":"overture:ga37_2009:4","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 22-5 and 22-6 to Add 'Interim Pastor'","year":2009,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga37_2009.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga37_2009.md","evidence_basis":"title_subject_reference","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-5--overture:ga37_2009:4:occ-a2fef652f3dc","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga37_2009.html#ga37-p273","repository_path":"markdown/ga37_2009.md#ga37-p273","locator":{"fragment":"ga37-p273","page":273},"excerpt":"Amend BCO 22-5 and 22-6 to Add 'Interim Pastor'","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga37_2009.md"}],"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 4 from Heritage Presbytery (to CCB, OC)"}},{"id":"bco:22-5--overture:ga06_1978:6","record_id":"overture:ga06_1978:6","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 22-5 to Allow Non-Presbytery